WEBVTT

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:06.195
A register sale is an order like any other.

00:00:06.195 --> 00:00:11.263
Open Commerce, Orders, and it is there, with a badge that names its register.

00:00:11.718 --> 00:00:14.492
The first list filters by channel:

00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:19.207
Every channel, Online, Point of sale, or Drafts sent by staff.

00:00:19.207 --> 00:00:22.328
The channel also limits the CSV export.

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:23.803
Open a sale.

00:00:23.803 --> 00:00:28.187
Nothing is shipped, because the buyer takes the goods with them, and it

00:00:28.187 --> 00:00:30.919
was taxed by the register's store address.

00:00:31.372 --> 00:00:35.626
Its stock came off the register's store, and the sale appears in your

00:00:35.626 --> 00:00:37.782
reports by store and by channel.

